Around 150 people already signed up for our webinar on Making it Work Financially in Israel. I&apos;m sharing some of the responses we got

&quot;I need answers.&quot;
&quot;I don&apos;t know how Israelis do it&quot;
&quot;To finally start saving money! Hhhh&quot;
&quot;To understand if I should stay in Israel or leave&quot;
&quot;I&apos;m curious to hear how everyone makes it in Israel&quot;
&quot;To understand how people afford life here and see if I can change anything&quot;
&quot;...even though I budgeted ... I&apos;m still having a very hard time making ends meet in Israel&quot;
&quot;I want to move to Israel, but honestly scared about the high cost of living vs low salaries&quot;
&quot;I can&apos;t for the life of me figure out how to prioritize my budget to allow saving for a vacation&quot;

The overwhelming response we got really confirms how pressing this topic actually is

That&apos;s why I&apos;m pumped that <a class="link" href="https://il.linkedin.com/in/nathan-joel?trk=public_post-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="public_post-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Nathan</a> and I will be hosting <a class="link" href="https://il.linkedin.com/in/rifkalebowitz?trk=public_post-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="public_post-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Rifka Lebowitz CFP®</a>, founder of the popular Facebook group Living Financially Smarter in Israel, on <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/next-million-hub?trk=public_post-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="public_post-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Next Million</a> on Tuesday, November 24

Rifka has helped thousands of Olim over the years crunch the numbers and her super-active group is one of my favorite spaces on FB

